 "final_text": "The file `/work/putnam_2000_b5.lean` now compiles with exit 0. There is no `sorry` warning and no errors. The only change to the theorem is `:=` became `:= by`, followed by the proof.\n\n**Proof idea:** Over `ZMod 2`, the XOR rule is addition, so the indicator polynomials satisfy `F(n+1) = (1+X)\u00b7F(n)`. Since `(1+X)^(2^m) = 1 + X^(2^m)` in characteristic 2, we get `F(2^m) = F(0) + X^(2^m)\u00b7F(0)`. Choosing `N = 2^(n+B)`, with `B` bounding `S 0`, makes `S 0` and `N + S 0` disjoint, so the XOR becomes the union.\n\nThe remaining warnings are only deprecations (`Xor'`, `finset_sum_coeff`, `Set.mem_setOf_eq`) and unused simp arguments. I did not clean them up.",
